github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105251#issuecomment-2813041348","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105251","id":2813041348,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nq5rE","user":{"login":"QbieShay","id":7917475,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MTc0NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7917475?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay","html_url":"https://github.com/QbieShay","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-17T14:03:08Z","updated_at":"2025-04-17T14:03:08Z","body":"This needs testing to check how it behaves compared to GPUParticles. Code here: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/c5c1cd4440a124f9a19898364b78ff7172755567/scene/resources/particle_process_material.cpp#L854\r\n\r\nGPUParticles set particles inactive at birth depending on a random value https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/c5c1cd4440a124f9a19898364b78ff7172755567/scene/resources/particle_process_material.cpp#L854\r\n\r\nThis gives it an organic feel while still maintaining that zero has no emission and 1 is full emission. Your PR kills one particle every X, which is not the same behaviour.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2813041348/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2813405751","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105251#issuecomment-2813405751","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105251","id":2813405751,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nsSo3","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-17T15:54:02Z","updated_at":"2025-04-17T15:54:12Z","body":"> This gives it an organic feel while still maintaining that zero has no emission and 1 is full emission. Your PR kills one particle every X, which is not the same behaviour.\r\n\r\nSee discussion in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104276. The \"kill one particle every X\" behavior seems more desirable overall, especially at low particle counts.\r\n\r\nThat said, we should aim for consistency between CPUParticles and GPUParticles, so this PR should be changed to use the random approach for now.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengi